{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>Only the tribe of Levi you shall not number.</b> The legion of the King is worthy of being counted on its own (Tanchuma). Another interpretation: the Holy One, blessed be He, foresaw that a decree was destined to fall upon all who were counted from twenty years old and upward, that they would die in the wilderness. He said: let these not be included, for they are Mine — they did not sin with the calf (ibid.; Bava Batra 121a)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:06.863645975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}